## Implementation

### Manifest composition and verification

- Added `core/pit_optimizer_v5/manifest.py` without redefining the accepted
  `CampaignManifestV5`, `SearchCapabilitiesV5`, `ProviderCapabilitiesV5`, or
  `ResourceCapabilitiesV5` contracts.
- Added `PolicySourceSnapshotV5` and `PolicyScopeDescriptorV5`. The policy-scope descriptor binds:
  the exact clean source commit; the exact ordered four editable policy paths and byte digests; the
  accepted baseline policy revision child reference; and the manifest's full-source-escape bit.
- Preserved the Task 1 baseline identity ruling. `CampaignManifestV5.baseline_policy_revision_ref`
  remains exactly equal to `BaselineParentAuthorityV5.policy_revision_ref`, and the create-only
  baseline descriptor is the existing `PolicyRevisionIdentityV5` value at that exact path. No
  wrapper or parallel baseline contract was introduced.
- Added explicit clean-source capture from an absolute source root and absolute Git executable.
  The implementation requires the declared commit to equal `HEAD`, requires a completely clean
  worktree, and hashes bytes read from that exact commit for the fixed editable paths. No PATH,
  current-directory, environment, or hard-coded repository path supplies source authority.
- `build_campaign_manifest_v5` authenticates each supplied root before typed loading, authenticates
  the typed raw PIT bundle and price-provenance edges through the panel plan, verifies all raw panel
  owners, validates all precomposition bindings, performs create-only descriptor/manifest writes,
  and then reauthenticates the complete resulting graph before returning.
- `authenticate_campaign_manifest_v5` calls the complete graph verifier before typed authority
  construction. It then binds exact target, panel, raw data, evaluator, execution, sandbox,
  baseline campaign, baseline source bundle, baseline policy, policy scope, source commit, and
  resource identities. It also requires `apply=false`, `qualification_allowed=false`, and
  `full_replay_allowed=false`.
- Baseline evidence is revalidated against the exact discovery plan/evaluator via the existing
  baseline parent authority path. Evaluator execution/sandbox/data/source identities and baseline
  policy/source identities must match the corresponding exact authenticated values.
- Sandbox resources must exactly equal manifest resources. Existing fixed sandbox invariants keep
  networking absent, root/source/data mounts read-only, output bounded write-only, and the image and
  runtime digest-pinned. No legacy two-hour timeout floor was added.
- Provider-free composition stores `provider=None`. Provider-authorized composition requires model,
  call, total-token, and per-role output-token caps together. `maximum_usd=None` remains an unlimited
  USD ceiling only and does not remove call or token caps.

### CLI and exports

- Added closed `build-manifest`, `verify-manifest`, and `render-command` parsers and dispatch. Every
  artifact dependency uses an explicit canonical relative path plus SHA-256 under one explicit
  absolute artifact root. Source root, Git executable, and source commit are explicit build inputs.
- Capability values are explicit manifest inputs with the accepted contract defaults: two parallel
  evaluations; one CPU; 1 GiB; 64 MiB output; 60-second mechanics; 180-second quick and role-call;
  600-second discovery episode; 30-minute round; five-hour campaign; and 60-second cleanup.
- `verify-manifest` and `render-command` authenticate the complete dependency graph before producing
  output. Their output is a canonical, content-free projection.
- Per the controller's binding interface ruling, `render-command` does not emit or imply a runnable
  production `run` command. It renders the authenticated target/search/provider/resource/source
  authorization with `adapter_composition="pending"` and `executable=false`. A later fixture or
  production composition task must bind an explicit adapter authority; Task 2 does not invent
  adapter arguments or widen the accepted manifest.
- Exported the new Task 2 value types and functions from `core.pit_optimizer_v5/__init__.py`.
- The existing generic canonical dataclass artifact codec already decodes the new descriptor and
  discovers its exact `ArtifactRefV5` child. No duplicate codec or artifact-reference grammar was
  added, and no artifact codec source change was necessary.

